WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.230
You won. I was watching.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.150
It was a good shoot.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.570
Okay.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.300
The finals is next.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.110
I know you can do it.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.530
Don't expect too much.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.730
Anyway, that guy... Tenma-kun, was it?

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.480
He's a good player too.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.910
If you don't stay focused, he'll steal your position.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.760
Tsurugi!

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.370
Are you coming back from seeing your brother?

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:46.280
Yeah.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.910
Thanks for coming today.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:54.150
I really do believe it was because of you that we got to win against Teikoku.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.910
Why are we assembling here at Teikoku again the day after?

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.430
Maybe they're going to do something to us...

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.780
Like what?

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.750
I don't know...

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.670
But Teikoku has four Seeds on their team.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.650
Have you heard anything, Otonashi-sensei?

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.870
No, nothing.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.030
Look at your coach, he ain't scared.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:04.940
Don't worry, guys.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.700
Kidou invited us to come over.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.100
There's someone he wants us to meet.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:16.070
Raimon Eleven, we've been waiting for you.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:17.220
Come on in.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:22.270
But what you witness past this point must be kept top secret.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.300
You there.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.580
That means no photography.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.520
Okay...

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.110
This feels kind of scary...

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:39.080
They <i>are</i>  going to do something to us...

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.300
C'mon, not a chance.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.620
I should let you guys know something first.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.540
I had a talk with Coach Kidou yesterday.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.450
I'm sorry for keeping quiet about it.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.480
We are the Resistance.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:05.590
I suppose you can call us the rebel army fighting against Fifth Sector.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:06.720
Rebel army?

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:10.270
Then what was all that talk about Teikoku being under their control?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:14.090
All an act to get into the enemy's innermost camp.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:20.550
I used today's match to unveil who among Teikoku's soccer club was a Seed sent in undercover.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:25.790
Normal conditions make it hard to determine who they are among the players, you see.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:32.500
It was all so I could build up Teikoku's soccer club as a rebel army.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:39.180
I was surprised when Fifth Sector switched the semi-final setups at the last minute...

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.260
But I figured that this was a good opportunity.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:46.760
Playing against Raimon, a school who continues to defy Fifth Sector,

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.730
would mean a game where the outcome hasn't already been agreed upon.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:55.690
Those not affiliated with Fifth Sector would be able to enjoy themselves in a long-awaited real match.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:00.310
But those who are responsible as Seeds would not feel that way.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:06.020
If Raimon were to push them back, they would receive pressure from Fifth Sector,

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:09.300
and their movements should gradually show agitation and dismay as a result.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:14.830
I could see who was a Seed from such a transformation.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:20.120
Now Teikoku Academy can completely be rid of Fifth Sector.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:24.300
So, were you able to spot the Seeds?

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:25.770
Yeah.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.770
I expect they will be leaving Teikoku very soon.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.970
I didn't know our game with Teikoku was for that objective...

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.870
I'm grateful to you guys.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.820
That passion you had... That's what real soccer is.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.860
It's a secret base!

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.030
I'm getting excited too!

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.780
You two are such kids.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:09.690
The person you'll be meeting with now is our leader for the Resistance.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:15.560
We're thinking of bringing about a revolution in the current soccer world with this man.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.000
Revolution?

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.100
That's a pretty mind-blowing feat.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.680
Why are you so taken aback?

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.920
Your team has already <i>begun</i>  to fight for the revolution.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.230
Coach Kudou!

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.000
Coach!

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.560
I'm glad you made it, everyone.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:45.090
I've been watching you play this whole time.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:49.330
Matsukaze, Nishizono, you've been working hard.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.510
That's <i>all</i>  these guys have been doing, working hard.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:55.370
Thanks to them, we were able to remember something important.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.690
Anyway, Kidou.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:06:59.740
What is this place?

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.730
The headquarters for the Resistance is up ahead.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:07.240
Then, does that mean the leader of the Resistance is Coach Kudou?

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.490
No, it isn't me.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.120
Hibiki-san!

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.410
Chairman Raimon! And Principal Hirai!

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.540
It's good to see you in good health, Otonashi-kun.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.220
I've been waiting for this moment to come.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.090
Long time no see, Endou.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:31.220
Yes, it's been awhile, Hibiki-san.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.260
That's <i>the</i>  Hibiki Seigou...

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.910
Why didn't any of you say something about this sooner?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.650
I apologize for that, Endou.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:48.900
We couldn't make any careless moves until all traces of Fifth Sector were completely wiped out from Teikoku.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:55.370
One mistake and they would be sure to notice our presence and obliterate us from the soccer world.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:00.430
If that were to happen, the revolution of the youth soccer association would be virtually impossible.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.410
So, about this revolution...

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:10.430
We will be taking from Fifth Sector's supreme ruler, Ishido Shuuji, the seat of the head of the youth soccer association...

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.920
In short, the seat of the Holy Emperor!

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.890
The Holy Emperor's seat?

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:21.850
We believe that by doing so, we can take back the free-spirited soccer of the past.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:30.590
The winning points of each match in Holy Road's Nationals tournament reflect the votes of one's supporters.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.880
The tournament itself is an election to decide the next Holy Emperor.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:40.660
We intend to make Ishido Shuuji drop out of the running and install Hibiki-san as the new Holy Emperor.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:46.850
You must win the final coming up and enter the Nationals tournament at any cost.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.420
Losing is no longer an option.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.960
We aren't thinking of losing anymore.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.570
In fact, this is quite reassuring.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:09:00.220
Now we know we weren't the only ones raising the signal for rebellion.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.560
This is getting big.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:09.510
Could we just be witnessing an important turning point in history?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.500
We sure are, full-on.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:21.040
I don't understand all that well yet what the adults are thinking about revolution and elections and such...

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:26.640
But what I did get is that we have to keep winning.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:31.270
And also, that everyone here loves soccer.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.650
Inazuma Eleven...

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:36.410
GO!

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.760
Inazuma Eleven...

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.100
GO!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.540
They've all changed.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.460
Yeah, they sure have.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:56.360
They've all got the faces of fighting men.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:02.070
Those who've decided something strongly within themselves have a good expression on their faces.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.310
They're stirring up a wind.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:05.620
A wind?

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:08.330
A wind blowing from Raimon.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.560
That's a cool thing to say.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.550
A wind...

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:19.010
This could in fact be the wind of revolution...

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.010
Kurumada-san, please do it.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:30.720
Something wrong?

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:32.570
No...

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:37.440
Raimon has begun training for the finals.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.830
The representative for B Block will be decided tomorrow, won't it?

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.830
It'll most likely be Kaiou Academy.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.950
What do we know about Kaiou Academy?

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.910
As of now, nothing.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:55.840
Since we'd progressed along B Block as ordered by Fifth Sector,

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:00.310
we are particularly lacking in knowledge of Kaiou Academy's true strength.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.530
Continue to gather information...

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.450
...and not just to help this revolution succeed.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.350
Also, Kidou.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:10.530
Yes?

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.240
I want to give you a new mission.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.820
3, 3, 3, 3!

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:36.250
All right!

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.350
Still haven't gone home yet?

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.570
Coach.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.970
Are you practicing on a hissatsu technique?

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:49.970
Yes.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:55.980
I couldn't sit still after thinking how we can't afford to lose anymore...

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:59.980
Don't you think you're overexerting yourself?

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.890
Still, I understand how you feel.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.970
I'm surprised too.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:06.960
It's a revolution!

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:13.920
I only did this too because I wanted to take back real soccer.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.500
I never guessed it would turn into something this big.

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.090
Yeah...

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.730
Seeing you took me back.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:30.600
I'd often continue practicing alone too, after regular practice was over.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.970
I wanted to get even stronger.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.600
I wanted to learn more and more amazing techniques.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.060
That's right!

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.680
I'm sure the opponents we face will get even stronger from here,

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:46.240
so if I learned a defense technique other than Soyokaze Step, I think it'll be useful in a lot of areas!

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.790
You're close. You're very close.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.540
You have your shoot technique, Mach Wind, don't you?

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.620
Isn't that enough?

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:58.590
I thought maybe I could use Mach Wind's speed for defense.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.830
I see...

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:02.110
So you want to rise up even higher.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.260
Yes!

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:06.720
In that case...

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:10.580
Why don't we make it together?

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:11.930
With you?

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.510
I'll be your opponent.

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:14.920
Try and steal the ball from me.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:16.940
Okay!

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:42.000
We thought you'd already left...

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:46.190
You think we're weird, don't you...

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:58.600
Well, why would I?

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:01.770
You were a part of the soccer club and all.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.690
Oh yeah, we went to see your game against Teikoku.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.370
Oh, thanks.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.990
It was a great match, with both teams giving it their all...

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:18.410
I think that may be the first time we'd ever seen a match that intense...

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:21.380
Also, that first-year Tsurugi...

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:26.460
I never thought he would be the one to master Ultimate Thunder.

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.630
He's a Seed from Fifth Sector, isn't he?

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:34.100
The person Tsurugi is now isn't the same Tsurugi from the Black Knights that you know.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:37.610
He's a part of the Raimon Eleven.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:41.980
We're going to the Nationals.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:44.900
The fight's already begun.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.860
Nothing can stop us and we don't plan on stopping.

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:49.740
Aren't you scared?

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:53.200
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't...

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:58.290
But I don't want to lie about my feelings for soccer.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.360
You almost had it that time!

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:13.190
But it's still not good enough.

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:16.300
I know. I still need more speed.

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:18.640
So you're starting to see what you need to work on.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.190
Let's stop here for today and pick it back up tomorrow!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.540
Okay.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:26.900
Thank you!

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:30.400
Say, want to drop by at my place? Have dinner!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.090
At your place?

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:34.280
Is that okay?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:35.680
Sure, come along!

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:44.190
It's me. I'm bringing us a guest.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:47.620
One of the soccer club members. Add another place mat at the table, 'kay?

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.740
Okay, let's go!

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.770
Um, who was that you were calling?

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:53.510
My wife.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.770
Coach, you're married?!

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:05.560
Hey, we're here!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.940
Welcome back, Endou-kun.

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:09.820
H-Hello!

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:12.550
I'm home!

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.250
Here's the guest I mentioned.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.020
Go on, introduce yourself.

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:18.330
You must be Matsukaze Tenma-kun.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:19.840
Yes!

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:22.970
Welcome! I'm Endou Natsumi.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:26.540
Endou-kun talks about you all the time, so I recognized you right away.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.260
You sure worked hard on this one!

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:38.270
Our guest is a growing boy, after all.

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.010
You can eat this much, can't you?

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:41.640
Yes!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:44.500
It all looks so good!

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.580
Thank you for the food!

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.320
Yeah, eat up!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.930
Food tastes the best after a hard workout!

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:02.540
How is it, Tenma-kun?

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:03.580
Does it taste good?

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:11.730
It's very good!

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.200
Thank goodness!

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.340
Then I'll bring some more!

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:18.260
Coach, this really tastes...

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.690
When you're a man, just don't say anything and chew.

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:22.990
As long as you think it tastes good, it'll work out somehow.

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:26.160
I don't think "working out somehow" quite works out that way.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.350
Here you go!

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:30.110
You have to eat a balanced meal!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.120
Okay!

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.030
I met your father today.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.080
That sure was a surprise.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.530
So you went down to Teikoku's basement.

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.750
You knew?

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.770
I heard about it from my father.

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:51.500
What, was I the only one left out of the loop?

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:54.060
I'm sorry for not telling you.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:18:00.760
In order for them to prepare for the revolution, it was convenient for it to be believed that Raimon began a solo rebellion.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.220
A solo rebellion, huh?

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:10.770
In doing so, all attention would focus on Raimon, allowing Kidou-kun and the others to move easier.

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:18.360
They were able to build their base in Teikoku and continue with preparations.

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.100
I see.

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:25.330
Well, as long as it helped them get ready, that's all right then.

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:28.540
Yes, it's all thanks to you.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.000
No, it wasn't me.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.540
It's all thanks to the Raimon Eleven.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.760
I couldn't have pulled off this revolution on my own.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:40.640
It's because everyone in Raimon thought twice about their feelings for soccer.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:48.360
Yes. The soccer that existed in your time is being passed on now to Tenma-kun and the others.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:49.140
Yeah.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.520
Let's do our best, Tenma.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.270
This fight still has a long way to go.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:56.750
Okay!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.540
Let's go, Tenma!

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:08.500
Okay!

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:12.460
Here goes!

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:16.210
Are you okay?

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:18.950
You should take a break.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:21.250
I'm fine.

00:19:22.380 --> 00:19:23.510
I can still go on.

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:27.130
I feel something bubbling inside of me.

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:32.580
It's like some power is bursting to come out as soon as possible.

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:34.550
A power bursting to come out?

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:37.360
It must be a hissatsu technique.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:42.280
So, I think if I keep training more and more, that power will come out!

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:45.900
He's making Soyokaze Step an even stronger wind?

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.490
He seems to have hit upon something, but...

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.670
The wind of Soyokaze Step...

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:55.470
Except faster, stronger!

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.420
I'll be like the wind!

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.280
All right, come on!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:08.890
Coach Endou, that's what happened on the first day as well!

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.390
Yeah...

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.880
I heard about it from Kudou-san, but...

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:17.220
Hey.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.540
Looks like what you said about a power hiding inside you is true.

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:23.050
What's this all of a sudden?

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:26.740
Coach, can I partner with him this time?

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:30.410
What are you planning to do?

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:35.510
I'll use my power to draw out the power that's sleeping inside of him.

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.260
If it'll help the team, I'll do it!

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:45.800
Okay, go for it.

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:48.310
Let's go.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:49.030
Okay!

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:54.220
Tsurugi, could you be thinking...?

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:07.830
I feel it coming...

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.700
I feel something coming inside me!

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:12.730
Here I go again.

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:13.500
Okay!

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:17.820
We'll definitely perfect this technique.

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:22.920
Forget it being a defense technique, something else incredible just might come out.

00:22:53.950 --> 00:22:57.180
Our opponent in Holy Road's final is Kaiou Academy!

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:59.850
What? All of them are Seeds?!

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:03.940
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 Ravaging Fangs Of The Sea Kings!

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:05.690
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:17.830
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:26.440
Those who've decided something strongly within themselves have a good expression on their faces!

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:27.280
That's all!
